cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you refer to this study or tool, please cite it as below, and cite the prior work it builds on."
title: "Evalplane: one policy sentence, three defensible readings, 35x apart"
abstract: >-
  A deterministic policy-coverage checker for LLM agents, and a calibration study over 4,448 published
  tau2-bench trajectories showing that the measured rate of policy violation depends on which defensible
  reading of a policy sentence the auditor encodes, by a factor of 35.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Kannaujia
    given-names: Vishnu
repository-code: "https://github.com/vishnukannaujia/evalplane"
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.0.dev0
date-released: "2026-10-04"
keywords:
  - agent-evaluation
  - llm-evaluation
  - policy-as-code
  - tau2-bench
references:
  - type: software
    title: "llmcontract-tau2: session-type contracts over tau2-bench trajectories"
    notes: "Published the underlying finding five months earlier; one point on the calibration curve."
